<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Williams (missionary)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1796">1796</a>–<a href="/years/1839">1839</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as John Williams</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Williams was an English Congregationalist missionary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a> who worked in the South Pacific from 1817. Based on Raiatea, he spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> through the Society, Cook and Samoan islands using Polynesian teachers, and visited Rarotonga in 1823 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papeiha">Papeiha</a>. He was killed on Erromango in the New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanuatu">Vanuatu</a>) in 1839 and became a celebrated missionary martyr.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-williams-missionary.jpg" alt="John Williams (missionary)" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Baxter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Rev._John_Williams,_the_Martyr_of_Erromanga,_with_a_landscape_of_the_Mission_House_and_grounds_of_Rarotonga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
